  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\beta-$ Ketoacids undergo decarboxylation easily. It is due to the stability of transition state formed after decarboxylation of $\\beta$-keto acids. This is not possible in case of other acids.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/G9onUPiY5nAanJf2o70Ze_djJIj72IOTdMvWWFJiWO8.original.fullsize.png\">",
